 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518163,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Brian deposits $5,600 in a savings account that yields 1.23% interest compounded annually. If he leaves that deposit in the account and adds nothing new to the account, what will the account be worth in 5 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The amount in the account, <i>A</i>, when the principal, <i>P</i>, is invested at an annual interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form), compounded <i>n</i> times per year for <i>t</i> years is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^{nt}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>It will help you get the right answer from your calculator to find <i>nt</i> separately.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"nt = \\left( 1 \\right)\\left( 5 \\right) = 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 5,600{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0123}}{1}} \\right)^5} = \\$5,952.97\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$5,952.97"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
